# 7. Complete presentations

<div class="code-path">Code: <code>tutorial/decks/reveal.js/</code>, <code>tutorial/decks/lhtml-site/</code></div>

The previous examples place one model in one slide. In a real talk, the models are mixed with the rest of the
presentation: a title, an outline, sections, slides of text, and from time to time a slide with a model next to
its text. The objective of this page is to show such a complete presentation.

The same talk of twelve slides is given twice: once made with reveal.js, and once made with lhtml-site. Both use
the models of the previous examples.

